From abfb1850fbe75c9c97b9cfb8430681709a68981c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:27:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Raise ci-red main_health for failed empty post-merge
 suites
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The no-required-check fallback appends a failed 0-run check suite created
after mergedAt to post_merge_checks inside fallback_outcomes, but
merge_evidence had already computed main_health from the earlier rows. A
failed empty suite on the landed sha (e.g. a main-push workflow with an
invalid workflow file) therefore never raised the ci-red pointer.

Fix: the main_health computation moves into flag_main_health(), which
merge_evidence still calls, and collect_acceptance calls it again after
fallback_outcomes. It only ever adds the pointer, so the second call is
idempotent; it is a no-op unless the PR merged as this exact head, and the
required-check path adds no post-merge rows after merge_evidence, so that
path's evidence and pointer are unchanged.

Red conclusion set (RED_CONCLUSIONS), decided here:
- red: failure, error, timed_out, action_required, and now startup_failure
  (the workflow could not start on the landed sha: real breakage, and the
  usual conclusion of a jobless failed suite).
- not red: cancelled (concurrency groups routinely cancel a superseded main
  run; already pinned by test_nonfailure_postmerge_checks_do_not_claim_main_is_red),
  stale, neutral, skipped, success, unknown/None.
main_health stays diagnostic only: ci-main-watch owns base health, and
acceptance classification is unchanged.

Follow-up to independent review t_01a1daf204b0b701 of PR #3036 (review
5906041934, nit 1). PR #3036 (landed as 95e3d3cf35) introduced the
post-merge empty-suite rows.

Proof:
- RED on origin/main 6b75e232c9 (code reverted, new tests kept): 5 failed —
  test_failed_empty_suite_after_merge_raises_main_health[failure,
  startup_failure, timed_out, action_required] and
  test_red_postmerge_conclusions_claim_main_is_red[startup_failure]. On
  main the empty-suite row is dropped entirely, so these fail there too.
- GREEN: all 18 test files importing kanban_pr_acceptance/merge_time/
  fallback: 515 passed, 1 skipped.
- Mutants killed: dropping the post-fallback flag_main_health call (4
  fail); dropping startup_failure from RED_CONCLUSIONS (2 fail).
- Negative controls pass: cancelled/stale/None empty suites and a failed
  empty suite on an unlanded (rebased) head raise no main_health.
- scripts/check --base origin/main: 20 checks ok.
